.SH NAME
ktm-term \- Colors written as markup, status lines, lined-up tables, a progress bar, and lines read with editing and a history, as GNU readline.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import term;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Colors written as markup, status lines, lined-up tables, a progress bar, and lines read with editing and a history, as GNU readline.
.SH TYPES
.SS Align
.EX
enum Align { left, right, center };
.EE
.PP
How a table column lines up. Without Table.align, a column of numbers is on the right and any other on the left.
.SS Border
.EX
enum Border { none, box, markdown };
.EE
.PP
How a table is drawn: plain columns, lines around every cell, or a Markdown table
.SS Progress
.EX
struct Progress {
    private u8[] label;
    private i64 total;
    private i64 count;
    private i64 started;
    private i64 drawn;
    private i64 shownPct;
    private bool live;
};
.EE
.PP
A progress bar on stderr, redrawn in place on a terminal. Lines written with term's functions while it runs go above it.
.SS Table
.EX
struct Table {
    Border border;
    private vec.Vec<String> cells;
    private vec.Vec<i64> starts;
    private vec.Vec<i64> kinds;
    private vec.Vec<i64> aligns;
    private i64 ncols;
};
.EE
.PP
A table: rows of cells under a header, in lined-up columns
